---Maintenance window as defined by Oracle. https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/api/#/en/database/20160918/datatypes/MaintenanceWindow
---@class gcp.oracledatabase_v1.MaintenanceWindow
---@field months? gcp.oracledatabase_v1.MaintenanceWindowMonthsItemEnumList Optional. Months during the year when maintenance should be performed.
---@field weeksOfMonth? gcp.oracledatabase_v1.IntegerList Optional. Weeks during the month when maintenance should be performed. Weeks start on the 1st, 8th, 15th, and 22nd days of the month, and have a duration of 7 days. Weeks start and end based on calendar dates, not days of the week.
---@field customActionTimeoutMins? number Optional. Determines the amount of time the system will wait before the start of each database server patching operation. Custom action timeout is in minutes and valid value is between 15 to 120 (inclusive).
---@field daysOfWeek? gcp.oracledatabase_v1.MaintenanceWindowDaysOfWeekItemEnumList Optional. Days during the week when maintenance should be performed.
---@field patchingMode? gcp.oracledatabase_v1.MaintenanceWindowPatchingModeEnum|string Optional. Cloud CloudExadataInfrastructure node patching method, either "ROLLING" or "NONROLLING". Default value is ROLLING.
---@field isCustomActionTimeoutEnabled? boolean Optional. If true, enables the configuration of a custom action timeout (waiting period) between database server patching operations.
---@field leadTimeWeek? number Optional. Lead time window allows user to set a lead time to prepare for a down time. The lead time is in weeks and valid value is between 1 to 4.
---@field preference? gcp.oracledatabase_v1.MaintenanceWindowPreferenceEnum|string Optional. The maintenance window scheduling preference.
---@field hoursOfDay? gcp.oracledatabase_v1.IntegerList Optional. The window of hours during the day when maintenance should be performed. The window is a 4 hour slot. Valid values are: 0 - represents time slot 0:00 - 3:59 UTC 4 - represents time slot 4:00 - 7:59 UTC 8 - represents time slot 8:00 - 11:59 UTC 12 - represents time slot 12:00 - 15:59 UTC 16 - represents time slot 16:00 - 19:59 UTC 20 - represents time slot 20:00 - 23:59 UTC

